From: PTPT52.AI <ptpt52@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 16:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: use DRAM LMGR descriptors on AN7563

The AN7563 vendor driver forces qdmaDscpMode to zero for the EN7523
family, selecting DRAM descriptor mode.  A register dump from the
working vendor firmware confirms QDMA_CSR_LMGR_INIT_CFG is 0x11804000,
with LMGR_SRAM_MODE bit 30 clear.

The upstream driver unconditionally sets LMGR_SRAM_MODE while starting
the hardware forwarding descriptor manager.  This selects a different
resource-manager layout on AN7563 and can prevent submitted TX
descriptors from completing.

Describe the LMGR mode in the SoC data and explicitly clear bit 30 for
AN7563.  Keep the existing SRAM mode on EN7581 and AN7583.

Signed-off-by: PTPT52.AI <ptpt52@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c | 4 +++-
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h | 1 +
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -1574,7 +1574,8 @@ static int airoha_qdma_init_hfwd_queues(
 			LMGR_INIT_START | LMGR_SRAM_MODE_MASK |
 			HW_FWD_DESC_NUM_MASK,
 			FIELD_PREP(HW_FWD_DESC_NUM_MASK, num_desc) |
-			LMGR_INIT_START | LMGR_SRAM_MODE_MASK);
+			LMGR_INIT_START |
+			(eth->soc->lmgr_dram_mode ? 0 : LMGR_SRAM_MODE_MASK));
 
 	return read_poll_timeout(airoha_qdma_rr, status,
 				 !(status & LMGR_INIT_START), USEC_PER_MSEC,
@@ -4514,6 +4515,7 @@ static const struct airoha_eth_soc_data a
 	.assemble_nbq = 15,
 	.rx_irq_bank1_mask = GENMASK(14, 10),
 	.has_rx_2b_offset = true,
+	.lmgr_dram_mode = true,
 	.ops = {
 		.get_sport = airoha_en7581_get_sport,
 		.get_dev_from_sport = airoha_en7581_get_dev_from_sport,
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
@@ -617,6 +617,7 @@ struct airoha_eth_soc_data {
 	int assemble_nbq;
 	u32 rx_irq_bank1_mask;
 	bool has_rx_2b_offset;
+	bool lmgr_dram_mode;
 	bool has_lro;
 	bool has_ppe_stats;
 	struct {
